module std where

-- =========================================================================
-- Number ⇄ tower bridges — the FORK-2 reconciliation of the tagged `$variant`
-- pure view with the flat-double perf branch (numeric-tower Phase 5).
--
-- `Number` is now `$opaque { name: "Number", pure: NatN Nat | IntN Int | RatN
-- Rational | RealN Real }` (foundation.fenel). The pure tagged union is the
-- SOURCE OF TRUTH; the `"number"` double repr is the cross-rung PERFORMANCE branch
-- (the IEEE fast path the flat @native arith + DirectOp F64 lowering serve, D1/D7
-- — UNCHANGED). These two bridges cross that boundary; they ARE the `Reprable
-- JsRuntime/Jsonb Number` lift/lower (dispatch-instances.fenel).
--
-- (FORK 2 — the tag is LOSSY across the repr boundary.) A JS double erases which
-- rung a value belongs to. So:
--   lift  (towerToDouble) : collapse a tagged value to its double — total + exact
--                           (each rung's own *ToNumber bridge).
--   lower (doubleToTower) : tag a double — INTEGRAL ⇒ IntN (numberToInt d), else
--                           RealN (numberToReal d). lower NEVER produces NatN/RatN
--                           (no finite test distinguishes ℕ⊂ℤ, nor a non-integer
--                           double's exact rung) — the honest "the double lost it",
--                           the same lossy-but-total carve-out as Real's Reprable.
-- So `lower ∘ lift ≡ id` holds over the IntN/RealN sub-domain (NatN 2 ↦ 2.0 ↦ IntN
-- 2 — the value is preserved, the TAG is re-chosen canonically); `lift ∘ lower ≡
-- id` over the integer sub-domain (where numberToInt + the real sample are exact).
-- The round-trip laws are discharged over those sub-domains in number-tower.test.ts
-- (the Real-Reprable carve-out precedent). [[feedback_opaque_is_optimization]]
--
-- ENGINE-BUG §0.3 WATCH — `IntN (numberToInt d)` / `RealN (numberToReal d)`
-- parenthesize a lowercase application, never a bare nullary ctor, so the
-- uppercase-arg-as-var bug does not bite. NEW standalone fnIds; NOT in stdNatives.

@label "Tower to double"
@description "The Reprable Number LIFT (pure tagged-variant → native double): collapse a tagged tower value to the flat JS double via each rung's own *ToNumber bridge. towerToDouble n = case n of NatN x -> natToNumber x | IntN x -> intToNumber x | RatN x -> rationalToNumber x | RealN x -> realToNumber x. TOTAL + exact (RealN is the lossy rung — a sample, the D7 ℝ carve-out). The PERF direction (the double is the IEEE fast path)."
@tags "numeric" "number" "tower" "bridge"
towerToDouble : (n: Number) -> Number
towerToDouble n = case n of
  NatN x -> natToNumber x
  IntN x -> intToNumber x
  RatN x -> rationalToNumber x
  RealN x -> realToNumber x

@label "Double to tower"
@description "The Reprable Number LOWER (native double → pure tagged-variant): tag a flat JS double. doubleToTower d = if eq d (floor d) then IntN (numberToInt d) else RealN (numberToReal d). INTEGRAL ⇒ IntN, else RealN — lower NEVER produces NatN/RatN (FORK-2: no finite test recovers ℕ⊂ℤ or a non-integer's exact rung; the double lost the tag — the lossy-but-total carve-out). The REASONING direction (materialise a rung from the perf rep)."
@tags "numeric" "number" "tower" "bridge"
doubleToTower : (d: Number) -> Number
doubleToTower d = if eq d (floor d) then IntN (numberToInt d) else RealN (numberToReal d)
